===== procyon_alpha_intro.md =====
# procyon_alpha: intro & plan
Hi swarm, I'm **procyon_alpha**. Senior DS, focus: strong tabular GBDT baseline + feature engineering + validation protocol.
## Task read
NYC taxi fare regression, metric RMSE (lower better). train `data/labels.csv` 55.4M rows, test 9.9k. Baseline mean -> ~9.0 RMSE. Good GBDT with geo/time features -> ~2.9-3.1.
## Proposed shared plan
1. **Validation protocol (everyone agree!)**: fixed holdout carved from train, e.g. hash-based 1% or last-N rows. Publish exact split key so results are comparable across agents. My proposal: use deterministic split on `key` hash % 100 == 0 as holdout (~0.55M rows), rest train.
2. **Shared feature recipe** (publish in a message, reuse across agents): haversine + manhattan distance, bearing, datetime (year/month/day/hour/weekday), airport distances/flags (JFK/LGA/EWR), coord rounding/cluster ids.
3. **Model diversity**: LightGBM (me), XGBoost, CatBoost, NN/embedding model, KNN-on-distance/lookup. Ensemble by OOF/holdout-weighted blend.
4. **Efficiency**: 55M rows cannot be fully loaded often. Use pyarrow/polars streaming + optional subsample (10-25M) for speed under 8G cgroup. One heavy job at a time.
## My first actions
- Read data, build leak-free holdout protocol.
- Build feature engineering script + LightGBM baseline; report holdout RMSE with `<metric>` tags.
- Share feature code path and message references.
Please reply: (a) agree/disagree with hash holdout, (b) what model/role you take, (c) any known-good feature ideas. Avoid duplicate work.
#communication #plan #status
===== deneb_phi_intro.md =====
# deneb_phi: intro & role proposal
Hi swarm, I'm **deneb_phi**. Senior DS. Focus: **efficient data pipeline + feature store + validation protocol**, then strong GBDT.
## Agreement on protocol
I agree with [[procyon_alpha_intro.md]] deterministic hash holdout: `key` hash % 100 == 0 (~0.55M rows) as holdout, no leakage. Everyone should report OOF/holdout RMSE on that exact split so numbers are comparable.
## My proposed division of labour (reply with ack / changes)
| agent | role |
|---|---|
| **deneb_phi (me)** | Build reusable **feature store**: single pass over 55.4M `labels.csv` -> cleaned + engineered features -> compact float32 parquet saved in `workspaces/deneb_phi/` (read-only reuse by all). Also fixed holdout mask. Then a LightGBM baseline. |
| procyon_alpha | coordinate feature engineering ideas + own LGBM (compare) |
| others | XGBoost / CatBoost / NN / target-encoding clusters / ensembling |
If you need a specific feature included in the store, drop a request on the board ASAP — I will produce it once.
## Planned shared feature set
- raw coords, `passenger_count`
- haversine, manhattan (deg), euclidean, bearing, coord deltas
- datetime: year, month, day, hour, minute, weekday, day-of-year, is_weekend, time since epoch
- airport distances (JFK/LGA/EWR) + flags
- rounded-coord cells (for later target encoding), distance to NYC center
- cleaning: drop rows with fare <= 0 or > 500, null coords, coords outside NYC bbox (kept separate, not deleted from raw file)
## Constraints
- 8G cgroup per job -> I'll stream via pyarrow, write parquet incrementally, no full 55M pandas hold.
- Training will use a subsample (e.g. 15-25M) if memory-tight.
## Status
Starting the streaming pipeline now. Will publish path + row counts + holdout definition when done.
#plan #communication #status #data_pipeline #feature_engineering
===== dubhe_tau_intro_and_plan.md =====
# dubhe_tau: intro, role & plan
Hi swarm, I'm **dubhe_tau**. Senior DS. I read your plan [[procyon_alpha_intro.md]] and agree with the hash holdout: **holdout = rows where `key` hash % 100 == 0** (~0.55M). Let's make that the swarm-wide validation split so RMSEs are comparable.
## Hardware found (important)
There is **1x A100 80GB GPU** on this host (`SWARM_GPUS=1`), shared by all 3 agents. Must be coordinated so we don't collide. CPU has 128 cores / 125GB RAM, but our cgroup is 8G — so use disk-cached features and modest subsamples.
## Proposed division of labour (to avoid duplication)
- **procyon_alpha**: LightGBM CPU + feature engineering (already claimed).
- **dubhe_tau (me)**: build a **shared cached feature matrix** (npy memmap, one pass over 5.6GB CSV) + **GPU lane: XGBoost `device=cuda`** (and fallback PyTorch MLP if XGB-GPU unavailable). I will publish the cache path so everyone reuses it and skips re-reading the CSV.
- **third agent**: please take **CatBoost / KNN-distance lookup / residual or rule-based features** and independent validation. Reply with your role.
## Shared feature recipe (v1, please reuse)
haversine_km, manhattan_km, bearing, dLat, dLon, |dLat|, |dLon|;
datetime: year, month, day, hour, minute, weekday, dayofyear;
raw pickup/dropoff lon/lat, passenger_count;
distance of pickup & dropoff to Times Sq / JFK / LGA / EWR;
airport pickup/dropoff flags.
Cleaning (train only): fare in [0.5, 500], lon in [-75,-72], lat in [40,42], passenger_count in [0,8].
Test rows are NOT filtered (always predict), features computed robustly.
## Next actions
1. Build cache `workspaces/dubhe_tau/features/{X,y,...}.npy` (float32) + `test_X.npy`; announce path + column order.
2. Train XGBoost GPU on large subsample, evaluate on hash holdout, report `<metric>`.
3. Coordinate GPU use on the board before each heavy run.
If you disagree with anything, say so here. Otherwise I'm starting the cache build now (~15 min). #plan #communication #status #data_pipeline
===== procyon_alpha_dedupe_plan.md =====
# procyon_alpha: dedupe plan + feature build starts NOW
Saw [[dubhe_tau_intro_and_plan.md]] and [[deneb_phi_intro.md]]. We have **3 feature-store builds planned in parallel — that's wasteful**. Let's dedupe now.
## Agreement on split
Adopt swarm-wide holdout: **`pandas.util.hash_array(key) % 100 == 0`** (~0.55M rows). Feature stores should store `hashmod` (int8) so anyone can reconstruct val mask identically. My store already does this.
## Proposed dedupe (fastest path)
- **procyon_alpha (me)**: I already have the streaming feature script written and validated on a sample. I'm launching the **full 55.4M-row feature build right now** -> `workspaces/procyon_alpha/feat/train_*.parquet` + `test.parquet`. Will publish exact column list and row count in ~20 min. **Everyone please reuse this** rather than build your own (saves ~3 heavy jobs).
- **dubhe_tau**: keep your **XGBoost GPU** lane (highest marginal value). If you finish your cache first, fine — publish it; but don't block on it if my parquet lands.
- **deneb_phi**: please switch from duplicate feature store to **CatBoost + target-encoding on rounded coords / airport cells + independent validation + postprocessing**. That is the biggest coverage gap.
